Fixed. The bug was in `src/sim.ts:43`.

**Change:** `if (foodSurplus >= 0)` → `if (foodSurplus > 0)`.

Population grew whenever the surplus was zero or positive, so a settlement merely breaking even (food produced = food consumed, surplus = 0) still grew by 1 each turn. Requiring a strictly positive surplus means population only grows when production exceeds consumption, matching the docstring ("grows by 1 if there was a food surplus").

Verified: `npm run test` (4/4 pass) and `npm run typecheck` both clean. Note the existing test suite doesn't cover `advanceTurn`, so that behavior is now untested — worth adding a regression test for the break-even case if you want coverage.


